  "solution": "The logic follows here is: **[(Sum of First number and second number × 3) - First number = Third number]**\n\nNow\n\nFor,** (3, 5, 21)**\n\n[__**(3 + 5)**__ × 3] - 3\n\n(__**8× 3**__) - 3\n\n__**24 - 3**__ = 21 = Third number.\n\nSimilarly, \n\nFor, (4, 2, 14)\n\n[(__**4 + 2**__) × 3] - 4\n\n(__**6 × 3**__) - 4\n\n__**18 - 4**__ = 14 = Third number.\n\nLet's check each option one by one:\n\noption 1. (6, 3, 12)\n\n[(__**6 + 3**__) × 3] - 6\n\n(__**9 × 3**__) - 6\n\n__**27 - 6**__ = 21\n\n21 ≠ 12\n\n**option 2. (8, 4, 28)**\n\n[(__**8 + 4**__) × 3] - 8\n\n(__**12 × 3**__) - 8\n\n__**36 - 8**__ = 28\n\n**28 = 28**\n\noption 3. (5, 2, 19)\n\n[(__**5 + 2**__) × 3] - 5\n\n(__**7 × 3**__) - 5\n\n__**21 - 5**__ = 16\n\n16 ≠ 19\n\n**option 4. (7, 1, 23)**\n\n[(__**7 + 1**__) × 3] - 7\n\n(__**8 × 3**__) - 7\n\n__**24 - 7**__ =17\n\n17 ≠ 23\n\n**Hence, 'option 2' is the correct answer.**",
